    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "It may sound like music to her -- I can do better with my teeth in a cold Shower. Click — click — click."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 613,
        "text": "Kiki, Galbraith said something to me once, -- something you ought to know. We were talking and he said that people were like that ball on the fountain at the hotel --they got pushed around by things bigger than themselves."
      }
